From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:35:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] XHCI X0: measured baseline + docs/plans/XHCI_PLAN.md

Phase X0 of the plan the 2026-10-19 audit names first (the north-star
USB 3.0 host controller). Docs-only; the baseline is measured, not
assumed.

The device contract is read out of the driver that must run on the
machine -- AuraLite-OS@main drivers/usb/xhci.c (90 KB, real
command/event/transfer rings): the class 0x0C/0x03/0x30 probe with
legacy INTx (PCI cfg 0x3C; no MSI), the CAPLENGTH/HCSPARAMS/
HCCPARAMS/DBOFF/RTSOFF register map, the exact 11-step bring-up
(halt -> HCRST -> CNR -> CONFIG -> DCBAA/scratchpads -> CRCR with a
cycle-carrying Link TRB -> ERST/IMAN/IMOD -> port power -> INTE|RUN ->
INTx registration -> PORTSC scan with strict RW1C discipline), the
command/event/transfer TRB set (No Op .. Set TR Dequeue; the guest
polls the event ring after the doorbell, so deterministic synchronous
completion is contract-legal), and the guest receipt strings the X5
lane pins.

QEMU identity measured (docs/specs/pci-ids + lspci): qemu-xhci =
1b36:000d rev 01, prog-if 30. Our machine today: no xHCI-class
function on bus 0 (baseline receipt: the guest prints "[xhci] no xHCI
controller found"); the defect ledger D1-D7 maps to phases X1
(register file) .. X5 (interrupter/ports/close-out).

Gates: make test rc=0, both SeaBIOS ISO lanes green (docs-only change;
the phase boundary rule stands). STATUS/ROADMAP/CHANGELOG updated in
this commit; patch 0076 follows.
